{
  "_readme": "Human-edited half of the quick reference sheet. build_sheet.py reads the BINDINGS from controls/input.map and from the AutoHotkey sources; this file only says what those cannot: labels, grouping, physical control names, what each layer control is MEANT to do (expect), and what is known to be inconsistent. Run tools\\controls-sheet\\build.ps1 after any edit. See README.md beside this file.",

  "title": "Interstate '76: controls quick reference",
  "subtitle": "i76-everywhere control map (WASD-style). This is not the 1997 key layout; the last page compares the two.",

  "groups": [
    {"id": "driving",   "label": "Driving",   "code": "D", "color": "#cfe2f7"},
    {"id": "weapons",   "label": "Weapons",   "code": "W", "color": "#f8d0cc"},
    {"id": "targeting", "label": "Targeting", "code": "T", "color": "#fbe7b0"},
